  "composition": {
    "method": "Fresh persistent worktree from main cc806, which includes Raster PR85. Three runtime files match the owner exactly. Composer was merged with git merge-file using current Raster 3fa70686, original ae2afa Composer, and owner modal 8e5ae300. The conflict-free result f14ce8d5 matches the independently prepared owner cache. Only four tracked runtime paths differ from cc806; the owner browser verifier was copied unchanged.",
    "owner_basis_difference": "One of 23 owner dependencies differs: business-creative.mjs changed from c03c3dff to the already accepted Raster follow-up 2fbf6229. The current render workflow was preserved. The other 22 dependencies match.",
    "raster_preservation": "All current-main Raster models, UI, CSS, Edge and SQL remain unchanged. Composer differs only in modal CSS and openModal lifecycle. The original owner five source, 23 dependency and 19 evidence hashes remain exact.",
    "authority_boundaries": "The Core prefix before Modal Focus Trap and suffix after Rate Limiting are byte-identical to cc806. The four-file diff is limited to modal CSS, semantics, lifecycle and keyboard file selection. Auth, API, session, permission, CSV parsing, consent and canonical writer behavior remain unchanged."
  },
  "source_review": {
    "helper": "The compatible trapFocus helper returns an idempotent disposer. The original single-trap API still releases previous bindings. Opt-in modal bindings retain parent traps, recalculate visible enabled controls, handle topmost Tab/Escape, focus empty dialogs and release disconnected dialogs. Scroll-lock ownership transfers correctly during out-of-order release, restoring the original overflow value. Viewport listeners are disposed.",
    "modules": "Composer, Calendar and Audience own their existing modal closers and reuse the shared helper. Focus returns to the opener only in the current scope. Account or workspace disposal removes private dialog DOM and releases the trap. Shared CSS provides 44px controls, 16px phone inputs, safe-area padding, bounded headers and footers, scrolling bodies and naturally sized template cards. Contacts preserves its permission copy and canonical import writer; its file button opens the real browser chooser by keyboard.",
    "raster_interaction": "Both the Suite helper and image editor lock body scrolling. Tests with the actual Core helper verify that closing, Escape, successful saving and scope disposal restore scrolling and preserve image/file scrubbing and recovery through the original request. No new editable store, provider or library is introduced."
  },
  "verification": {
    "focused": "28 existing Core session, Composer AI and Email persistence tests passed with zero skips.",
    "suite": "20 independently repeated browser groups passed at 390px and 1440px widths with 390px height. They cover populated and sparse templates, CSV previews and posting queue; invalid CSV recovery; permission copy; keyboard file chooser; dynamic Tab/Escape and opener focus; nested, empty, out-of-order, legacy and disconnected traps; account/workspace disposal; and Contacts to the existing inline Email editor. No writes or provider/network operations were performed.",
    "extra_short": "Six additional 240px-high cases passed: Composer, Calendar and Audience at both 390px and 1440px widths. The 44px header remains visible, dialog bounds fit the viewport, scrolling bodies retain positive height, Tab stays inside, the focused file chooser is visible, and closing restores scrolling without horizontal overflow. Browser viewport resizing is not OS keyboard evidence.",
    "raster_original": "The existing 30 real PostgreSQL groups and 58 checks, including nine mounted Composer/Canvas/Edge/canonical-asset journeys, passed on the combined source. These use actual PostgreSQL16 contracts with synthetic SID rows and controlled local Auth/Storage HTTP transport; they are not live Supabase upload evidence.",
    "raster_actual_core": "The original Raster fixture omits zoi-core. An additional private helper loads the exact candidate Core and asserts that the shared helper runs by checking its visual-viewport CSS variable. All nine mounted journeys and 30 PostgreSQL groups passed again. The extra 390\u00d7240 image editor check confirms a visible 44px header and footer close action, keyboard crop, Escape, focus/scroll return, account/SID/workspace scrubbing, creation, reopen, rerender, caption editing and lost-response recovery.",
    "helper_setup_failures": "Relocating the private extra fixture initially caused two missing relative-import errors after five PostgreSQL setup groups. These were reviewer harness setup failures. The failed logs are retained. All remaining imports were then normalized against the original fixture location and the final run passed. No assertions or production authority checks were weakened.",
    "visual": "The reviewer viewed independent 390px populated Contacts and Templates screenshots and the 240px image editor screenshot. Controls and cards are aligned; headers and footers remain reachable while bodies scroll. The reported dark/light and sparse cases were exercised, without claiming complete device or theme certification.",
    "static": "All four runtime files pass node --check; git diff --check passes."
  },
  "commands": {
    "suite": "ZOI_SUITE_MODAL_EVIDENCE=<distinct>/browser node tests/browser/suite-modal-usability.mjs",
    "focused": "node --test tests/unit/core-session.test.mjs tests/unit/composer-ai.test.mjs tests/unit/email-persistence.test.mjs",
    "raster": "STUDIO_RASTER_BROWSER=1 ZOI_STUDIO_RASTER_EVIDENCE=<distinct>/raster PGPORT=15782 node tests/database/studio-raster.integration.mjs",
    "short": "ZOI_SUITE_MODAL_EVIDENCE=<distinct>/short node <private>/short-suite.mjs",
    "actual_core": "STUDIO_RASTER_BROWSER=1 ZOI_STUDIO_RASTER_EVIDENCE=<distinct>/raster-core-verified PGPORT=15782 node <private>/raster-core.integration.mjs"
  },
  "production_actions": [],
  "remaining": [
    "Root must copy the exact four runtime files, run protected CI, deploy, verify served hashes and exercise actual authenticated Suite journeys.",
    "Actual published-business owner Raster upload, reopen, recovery and cleanup remain open. Synthetic isolated owner fixtures do not close that production context gap.",
    "OS keyboard, physical safe areas, assistive technology and native app acceptance are unclaimed.",
    "Camera API reliability and the landscape Saved-pointer issue remain separate open queues."
